MSG_ROOT="Run this as the administrator: sudo flightgear-data-installer"
MSG_BUSY="Another run of flightgear-data-installer is working. Wait for it to end, then run: sudo flightgear-data-installer"
MSG_USAGE="Usage: flightgear-data-installer [install] [--file FILE] | --check | --purge"
MSG_TOOL="FlightGear's data was not installed: the program %s is missing. Nothing was changed. What to do: sudo apt install %s, then run: sudo flightgear-data-installer"
MSG_DOWNLOADING="Downloading FlightGear's data %s (%s) from FlightGear's release page on SourceForge. The file is large; this takes a while."
MSG_RESUMING="Continuing an earlier download of FlightGear's data (%s of %s are already here)."
MSG_PROGRESS="Downloaded %s of %s (%s%%)."
MSG_DOWNLOAD="FlightGear's data could not be downloaded from %s (%s). Nothing was installed. What to do: connect to the internet and run: sudo flightgear-data-installer (or: sudo dpkg --configure flightgear-data-installer). A partly downloaded file is kept in %s and the next run continues from it. On a computer without internet: download %s on another computer and run: sudo flightgear-data-installer --file FILE"
MSG_VERIFYING="Checking the file against the SHA-256 recorded in this package."
MSG_PRESENT="FlightGear's data %s is already installed in %s; nothing to download."
MSG_USING_FILE="Using the file %s."
MSG_FILE="The file %s cannot be read. Nothing was installed. What to do: give the path of the downloaded FlightGear data file: sudo flightgear-data-installer --file FILE"
MSG_SPACE="There is not enough free space in %s: %s are needed and %s are free. Nothing was installed. What to do: free that space, then run: sudo flightgear-data-installer"
MSG_HASH="The downloaded file does not match the SHA-256 recorded in this package (it is %s, expected %s), so it was not used. It was deleted and nothing was installed. What to do: run again to download it again: sudo flightgear-data-installer. If the same happens, report it at https://github.com/Sparky-OS/sparky-stereo-os/issues"
MSG_HASH_FILE="Your file does not match the SHA-256 recorded in this package (it is %s, expected %s), so it was not used. Your file was not changed and nothing was installed. What to do: download FlightGear's data file again, or run without --file to let this package download it: sudo flightgear-data-installer"
MSG_UNPACKING="Unpacking FlightGear's data into %s. This takes a few minutes."
MSG_UNPACK="FlightGear's data could not be unpacked (%s). The partly unpacked files were removed and nothing was installed. What to do: check the free space and the disk, then run: sudo flightgear-data-installer"
MSG_VERSION="The data says it is version %s, but %s was expected. Nothing was installed. What to do: report it at https://github.com/Sparky-OS/sparky-stereo-os/issues"
MSG_CONFLICT="FlightGear's data was not installed: %s already exists and does not come from this package (for example from the Debian packages flightgear-data-base, flightgear-data-ai or flightgear-data-models). Nothing was changed. What to do: remove the other package or that file, then run: sudo flightgear-data-installer"
MSG_DONE="FlightGear's data %s is installed in %s."
MSG_KEPT="The downloaded file stays in %s, so the next run does not download it again."
MSG_SETTING="The setting PARALLEL in /etc/default/flightgear-data-installer is \"%s\", but it must be a whole number from 1 to 16. Nothing was installed. What to do: correct that line, then run: sudo flightgear-data-installer"
